                EHM/MRO  DATA SET RECORD LAYOUTS
                ================================

                RELEASE 4.2C            09-FEB-1996

ALL FOUR DATA SETS ARE SEQUENTIAL CARD IMAGE FILES OF EIGHTY COLUMNS.
FIELDS ARE FIXED POSITION.  A CARD WITH AN ASTERISK IN COLUMN ONE IS A
COMMENT AND IS IGNORED BY THE LOADER.  A SHORT CARD IS PADDED WITH
BLANKS.  ANYTHING BEYOND COLUMN EIGHTY IS DISCARDED.

COLUMN NUMBERS BELOW ARE ONE RELATIVE.  THE OFFSETS COMPILED INTO THE
LOADER ARE ZERO RELATIVE AND ARE IN INCLUDE/DBIO.H.


1.  FLEET MASTER  -  FLEET.DAT
    --------------------------

    COL     WIDTH   FIELD
    -----   -----   ----------------------------------------------
     1- 8      8    ENGINE SERIAL NUMBER, LEADING ZEROES, KEY
    10-15      6    ENGINE MARK
    17-23      7    AIRFRAME REGISTRATION
    25-28      4    OPERATOR CODE
    30-36      7    HOURS SINCE NEW, RIGHT JUSTIFIED
    38-44      7    CYCLES SINCE NEW, RIGHT JUSTIFIED
    46-49      4    BUILD STANDARD
    51         1    SERVICEABILITY  S SERVICEABLE
                                    W ON WATCH
                                    R RESTRICTED
                                    U UNSERVICEABLE
    53-58      6    SHOP VISIT DUE, YYMMDD

    A CARD WITH A BLANK SERIAL NUMBER IS REJECTED AND COUNTED.  AN
    UNRECOGNISED SERVICEABILITY CODE IS REPORTED AND TAKEN AS S.


2.  FLIGHT REPORTS  -  FLIGHTS.DAT
    ------------------------------

    ONE CARD PER CRUISE SNAPSHOT.  THE OVERNIGHT EXTRACT WRITES THE
    FILE IN DATE ORDER WITHIN ENGINE AND THE LOADER RELIES ON THAT
    ORDER FOR THE HISTORY LISTING.

    COL     WIDTH   FIELD
    -----   -----   ----------------------------------------------
     1- 8      8    ENGINE SERIAL NUMBER
    10-15      6    FLIGHT DATE, YYMMDD
    17-22      6    FLIGHT NUMBER
    24-27      4    EXHAUST GAS TEMPERATURE, DEG C
    29-32      4    EGT MARGIN, DEG C
    34-37      4    N1 FAN SPEED, PER CENT TIMES TEN
    39-42      4    N2 CORE SPEED, PER CENT TIMES TEN
    44-48      5    FUEL FLOW, KG PER HOUR
    50-52      3    OIL PRESSURE, PSI
    54-56      3    OIL TEMPERATURE, DEG C
    58-60      3    BROADBAND VIBRATION, UNITS TIMES TEN
    62-68      7    CYCLES SINCE NEW AT THE TIME OF THE REPORT

    A CARD FOR AN ENGINE THAT IS NOT IN THE FLEET MASTER IS DROPPED
    AND COUNTED IN MESSAGE EHM-102.  THE EXTRACT ALWAYS CARRIES A FEW
    OF THESE FOR ENGINES SOLD OR SCRAPPED SINCE THE LAST MASTER
    REFRESH.


3.  WORKSHOP SLOTS  -  SLOTS.DAT
    ----------------------------

    ONE CARD PER SHOP PER WEEK COMMENCING.

    COL     WIDTH   FIELD
    -----   -----   ----------------------------------------------
     1- 4      4    SHOP CODE
     6-11      6    WEEK COMMENCING, YYMMDD, MONDAY
    13-14      2    BAYS AVAILABLE IN THAT WEEK

    A CARD WITH A BLANK SHOP CODE OR AN INVALID WEEK COMMENCING DATE
    IS REJECTED WITH MESSAGE EHM-920.


4.  SPARES AND ROTABLE POOL  -  SPARES.DAT
    --------------------------------------

    ONE CARD PER STOCKED PART NUMBER.  A PART NUMBER IS CARDED ONCE
    FOR EACH ENGINE MARK IT FITS AND ONCE FOR EACH WORKSCOPE THAT
    CONSUMES IT.

    COL     WIDTH   FIELD
    -----   -----   ----------------------------------------------
     1-10     10    PART NUMBER
    12-35     24    PART DESCRIPTION
    37-42      6    ENGINE TYPE THE PART FITS
    44-47      4    WORKSCOPE THAT CONSUMES IT, INSP HSR PERF OVHL
    49-52      4    QUANTITY ON HAND
    54-57      4    QUANTITY ON PURCHASE ORDER
    59-61      3    LEAD TIME IN DAYS
    63-63      1    POOL INDICATOR, R ROTABLE OR C CONSUMABLE

    THE WORKSCOPE MNEMONICS ARE THE ONES PRINTED BY THE INDUCTION
    PLAN AND HELD IN SRC/WRKSCD.C.  A CARD WITH A BLANK PART NUMBER,
    A BLANK ENGINE TYPE, A WORKSCOPE THAT IS NOT ONE OF THE FOUR
    ABOVE, OR A NEGATIVE QUANTITY IS REJECTED WITH MESSAGE EHM-926.
    AN UNRECOGNISED POOL INDICATOR IS REPORTED WITH EHM-927 AND THE
    PART IS TAKEN AS CONSUMABLE.  A NEGATIVE LEAD TIME IS TAKEN AS
    ZERO WITHOUT COMMENT.  THE TABLE HOLDS MAXSPR PARTS AND A LONGER
    FILE IS TRUNCATED WITH EHM-925.


5.  SCALING
    -------

    THE SYSTEM HOLDS NO FLOATING POINT.  QUANTITIES CARRIED TO ONE
    DECIMAL PLACE ARE STORED AS TENTHS

        N1, N2                  PER CENT TIMES TEN
        VIBRATION               UNITS TIMES TEN
        DETERIORATION RATE      DEG C PER THOUSAND CYCLES TIMES TEN

    THE PRINTED REPORTS SHOW THE SCALED INTEGER, NOT THE DECIMAL.  THE
    CONTROLLERS ARE USED TO READING IT THAT WAY.
